I fixed #1115 and committed it as 7dd69207. On -p and piped runs, a network error is now one readable line, and the hint no longer says /retry. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and fmt check all pass.

Before, on a refused non-loopback address, which is the case that prints the hint:
```
error: Network error: reqwest::Error { kind: Request, url: "http://10.1.1.37:9/v1/chat/completions", source: hyper_util::…ConnectError("tcp connect error", …, Os { code: 111, … message: "Connection refused" })) }
💡 Network error — could not reach the API.
     Check your --base-url value.
     You can retry with /retry.
```
After, on the built binary:
```
error: Network error: could not connect to http://10.1.1.37:9/v1/chat/completions (connection refused)
💡 Network error — could not reach the API.
     Check your --base-url value.
```
A DNS failure now reads could not connect to http://nonexistent.invalid/v1/chat/completions (dns error: failed to lookup address information: Name or service not known). With --verbose, the full raw error follows as a dimmed line.

What changed:
• New module `src/prompt/network_error_summary.rs`:
  • network_error_summary builds the one-line message. Any text that isn't a reqwest error dump prints exactly as before.
  • hint_for_surface removes the /retry line on -p and piped runs. It uses the existing is_single_shot() flag that main.rs already sets for both, so I added no new global.
  • The tests cover the issue's error string word for word, a DNS failure, text that should pass through unchanged, a URL with multi-byte characters, and the REPL hint, which is checked against its full text and is unchanged.
• `src/prompt_retry.rs` stays at 2786 lines. I replaced the /retry text with a constant from the new module, so the line that gets removed can't drift from the line that gets added.
• The plan was wrong about one file: the raw error is printed from src/prompt.rs, not prompt_retry.rs. I changed its six error lines in place and added two lines (mod and use), so it went from 3934 to 3936. I raised its entry in tests/module_size.rs to match, with the reason in a comment.
• Measured before editing: at HEAD, the loopback address (127.0.0.1:9) already printed a clean line through loopback_refused. The DNS failure printed the raw dump with no 💡 hint at all, because the hint only recognises other wordings of a DNS failure.
• No doc quoted the old text, so there were no doc changes.

Still open: these are noted as comments on open issues, since this push closes #1115.
• The billing and model-not-found hints still name REPL-only commands (/provider, /model) on -p. That's on #1086, and the same hint_for_surface function is where they'd be fixed.
• DNS failures still get no 💡 hint. That's on #1120, next to the separate problem of the ~73s of retries.
  ✓ Watch passed: `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test`
